+---
+type: spec
+task_slug: parse-duration-contract
+status: approved
+created: 2026-10-15
+tags: [timeparse, spec, python, parsing, input-contract]
+test_framework: pytest
+interview_rounds: 0
+lane: light
+summary: "Input contract for timeparse.parse.parse_duration: whitespace, sign, ASCII digits, 2**63-1 cap"
+---
+
+# SPEC: parse_duration input contract
+
+## 🎯 Intent
+`parse_duration` in `timeparse/parse.py` currently leans on `str.strip()`, `\d` and `int()`, which
+accept any Unicode whitespace and any Unicode decimal digit, and it has no upper bound on the total.
+The caller supplied an exhaustive input contract; this SPEC pins it so behavior is explicit and testable.
+
+## 🌅 Outcomes
+Every input class below is accepted or rejected exactly as listed. Any input not in a listed class
+behaves as it does today (unit case-insensitivity, largest-first unit order, no repeated units,
+no inner whitespace, unknown units rejected).
+
+## 📋 In-Scope Scenarios
+
+### S1: Surrounding ASCII whitespace is ignored
+**Given** a duration wrapped in spaces, tabs or newlines
+**When** `parse_duration` is called
+**Then** `" 1h\t"` returns 3600 and `"\n45s\n"` returns 45
+
+### S2: Other whitespace is rejected, also around the text
+**Given** a string with a non-ASCII-space whitespace character before or after the text
+**When** `parse_duration` is called
+**Then** `" 1h"` and `"1h "` raise `ValueError`
+
+### S3: A sign is rejected
+**Given** a string containing `+` or `-`
+**When** `parse_duration` is called
+**Then** `"+1h"`, `"-1h"` and `"1h-30m"` raise `ValueError`
+
+### S4: Only ASCII digits are digits
+**Given** a string using Arabic-Indic or fullwidth digits
+**When** `parse_duration` is called
+**Then** `"١h"` and `"１h"` raise `ValueError`
+
+### S5: Leading zeros are allowed
+**Given** a number with leading zeros
+**When** `parse_duration("007s")` is called
+**Then** it returns 7
+
+### S6: Total is capped at 2**63 - 1 seconds
+**Given** a duration whose total seconds is at or above the cap
+**When** `parse_duration` is called
+**Then** `"9223372036854775807s"` returns 9223372036854775807
+**And** `"9223372036854775808s"`, `"106751991167301d"` and `"106751991167300d16h"` raise `ValueError`
+
+### S7: Empty or all-whitespace input is rejected
+**Given** an empty or all-whitespace string
+**When** `parse_duration` is called
+**Then** `""` and `" \t\n"` raise `ValueError`
+
+## 🚫 Non-Goals
+- No change to unit set, unit order, repeat rules, case-insensitivity, or inner-whitespace handling.
+- No change to `timeparse` modules other than `parse.py`.
+- No new error types or messages contract (only `ValueError`).
+
+## ⚠️ Constraints
+| Constraint | Value | Rationale |
+|---|---|---|
+| Test framework | `pytest` | Existing `tests/test_parse.py` uses it |
+| Compatibility | Python as already supported by the repo | No new dependency |
+| Performance | none | Not a stated concern |
+
+## 🔒 Irreversible Decisions
+none
+
+## ✅ Verification Criteria
+| Scenario | Verification mode | Test name / manual step |
+|---|---|---|
+| S1 | unit | `test_surrounding_ascii_whitespace_ignored` |
+| S2 | unit | `test_other_whitespace_rejected` |
+| S3 | unit | `test_sign_rejected` |
+| S4 | unit | `test_non_ascii_digits_rejected` |
+| S5 | unit | `test_leading_zeros_allowed` |
+| S6 | unit | `test_total_cap` |
+| S7 | unit | `test_empty_and_blank_rejected` |
+
+### AC-001: Surrounding ASCII whitespace ignored
+Covers S1. Oracle: golden values taken verbatim from the caller's contract.
+
+### AC-002: Other whitespace rejected
+Covers S2. Oracle: golden inputs from the caller's contract.
+
+### AC-003: Sign rejected
+Covers S3. Oracle: golden inputs from the caller's contract.
+
+### AC-004: Only ASCII digits accepted
+Covers S4. Oracle: golden inputs from the caller's contract.
+
+### AC-005: Leading zeros allowed
+Covers S5. Oracle: golden value from the caller's contract.
+
+### AC-006: Total capped at 2**63 - 1
+Covers S6. Oracle: golden values from the contract; boundary arithmetic checked by hand
+(106751991167300 * 86400 + 16 * 3600 = 9223372036854777600 > 2**63 - 1).
+
+### AC-007: Empty or blank input rejected
+Covers S7. Oracle: golden inputs from the caller's contract.
+
+## ❓ Open Questions
+(none)
+
+## 🔍 Refinement Decisions
+- Lane `light`: one file, one session, no irreversible decision. Contract is exhaustive, so no interview rounds were needed (autopilot `auto_full`, no question asked).
+- "Spaces, tabs and newlines" is read as ASCII space, `\t`, `\n` and `\r` (`\r` kept ignored, as today, as part of a line ending). `\v`, `\f`, `\x1c`-`\x1f`, `\x85` and all Unicode whitespace raise `ValueError` as "other whitespace".
+- The cap applies to the total after summing all units, not per unit.
+- Spec-validator not dispatched: light lane, `irreversible_decisions: []`, ACs imply no irreversible category.
